@title Ferry Ticketing Platform
@subtitle Online ticketing on Azure, North Europe
@author Digital Channels, Owner
@date Reviewed 2026-09-22

# Overview
Passengers book through Azure Front Door. Every booking is written to one database and announced as an event, so the scanners at the terminals stay in step.

# Diagram
diagram azure dir=TB title="Ticketing platform, North Europe"
azure: pax "Passengers" user
azure: fd "Front Door" lb
azure: web "Booking Web App" svc
azure: api "Ticketing API" svc focus
azure: db "Reservations DB" db "Azure SQL"
azure: bus "Booking Events" queue "Service Bus"
azure: scan "Port Terminal Scanners" ext
azure: pay "Payment Provider" ext
azure: pax -> fd : HTTPS
azure: fd -> web : origin request
azure: web -> api : REST
azure: api -> db : SQL, port 1433
azure: api -> pay : card authorization
azure: api -> bus : ticket issued
azure: bus -> scan : sync every 30 s
azure: group appsn "App subnet 10.50.1.0/24" web, api
azure: group datasn "Data subnet 10.50.2.0/24" db, bus
azure: group vnet "Ticketing VNet 10.50.0.0/16" appsn, datasn
azure: group sub "Ticketing subscription" vnet

# Capacity
table = Component,Capacity; Booking Web App,"3 to 10 instances, scales at 60% CPU"; Ticketing API,4 to 16 pods; Reservations DB,"8 vCores, read replica in the paired region"

# Recovery targets
kpi Recovery point objective | 5 min | max data loss | neutral
kpi Recovery time objective | 1 hour | max downtime | neutral
kpi Last tested | 2026-08-19 | recovery drill | neutral
